@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-10-15
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Machine Keys
  "Manages which machines may publish: lists, adds, and removes public keys in the mason user's authorized_keys, identified by comment and SHA256 fingerprint."

  Provides:
    - setup.AuthorizedKey @source("symbol:AuthorizedKey")
    - setup.ParsePublicKey @source("symbol:ParsePublicKey")
    - setup.KeyList @source("symbol:KeyList")
    - setup.KeyAdd @source("symbol:KeyAdd")
    - setup.KeyRemove @source("symbol:KeyRemove")

  Consumes:
    - remote.CommandRunner

  Invariants:
    - All operations MUST run as the mason user on its own authorized_keys; none MUST need an admin
    - KeyAdd MUST validate the key (known type, decodable blob whose embedded type matches) before touching the server
    - KeyAdd MUST be idempotent (a key already present, with any options, is not added twice) and MUST install with the restrict options
    - Fingerprints MUST match OpenSSH's SHA256 format so they can be compared with ssh-keygen -lf
    - KeyRemove MUST match exactly one key by comment or fingerprint, and MUST refuse to remove the last key or the key this machine is using unless forced
    - KeyRemove MUST rewrite authorized_keys atomically and keep mode 600
    - Lines that are not keys (comments, blanks) MUST be preserved on rewrite

  OutOfScope:
    - Bootstrapping the first key (setup.BootstrapScript, as an admin)
    - Local key generation (setup.Keygen)

  Scenario (happy-path): Authorize a second laptop
    Given a valid public key line with comment mason@laptop2
    When KeyAdd runs from an authorized machine
    Then the key is appended with the restrict options and KeyList shows mason@laptop2

  Scenario (negative): Malformed key
    Given "ssh-ed25519 notbase64"
    When KeyAdd runs
    Then it fails without running any remote command

  Scenario (negative): Removing this machine's key
    Given the match names the key this machine uses
    When KeyRemove runs without force
    Then it refuses and the file is unchanged

  Scenario (edge): Ambiguous comment
    Given two keys with the same comment
    When KeyRemove runs with that comment
    Then it fails asking for the fingerprint instead
